{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Before the veil of the testimony.</b> That is before the ark, which is called 'testimony.' And our Sages expounded this of the western lamp, which is a testimony to all who come into the world that the Shekhinah dwells in Israel — for he puts in it oil like the measure of its fellows, and with it he would begin and with it he would end (Shabbat 22; Menachot 86)." "<b>Shall Aaron arrange it from evening to morning.</b> He shall arrange it with an arrangement suited to the measure of the entire night. And the Sages reckoned half a log for each and every lamp, and they suffice even for the nights of the season of Tevet, and this measure was fixed for them (Menachot 89)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:03.636267071Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}